# Requirement: Browser Extension for Local Bug Report Capture

## Goal

We want to test JavaScript code as a browser extension to support structured bug reporting.

The extension shall provide a browser button that allows the user to create a bug report for the currently active page. The user clicks the button after observing a bug. Since the user may not know how to reproduce the issue, the extension shall continuously keep a small local history of recent technical events and user interactions.

The generated bug report shall be exported as a downloadable JSON file.

## Core Concept

The extension shall run locally in the browser and maintain a limited in-memory event history for the active tab.

When the user clicks the bug report button, the extension shall export the current page context together with the recently captured event history.

The purpose is to provide enough context to help developers understand and reproduce the bug without recording user content, personal data, credentials, secrets, or sensitive information.

## Captured Page Metadata

The bug report shall include the following metadata:

* Current page URL
* Browser user agent
* Viewport size
* Screen resolution
* Current scroll position
* Current zoom level, if technically available
* Timestamp of bug report creation
* Extension version
* Browser name and version, if technically available

## Local Interaction Buffer

The extension shall maintain an in-memory ring buffer for the active tab.

The buffer shall contain:

* The last 50 relevant user interactions, or
* The last 5 minutes of relevant user interactions,

whichever is smaller.

Relevant interactions include:

* Click events
* Submit events
* Change events, without storing field values
* Route or navigation changes
* Selected high-level keyboard actions, without storing typed characters
* Scroll position snapshots
* Viewport resize events

Each captured interaction shall include:

* Timestamp
* Event type
* Current URL
* Sanitized target selector
* Target tag name
* ARIA role, if available
* Sanitized visible label, if explicitly allowed
* Viewport coordinates for click events
* Current scroll position

## Events That Must Not Be Captured

The extension shall not capture or store:

* Mouse movement events
* Pointer movement events
* Raw keypress events
* Typed characters
* Form field values
* Password field values
* Clipboard contents
* Full DOM snapshots
* Screenshots
* Video recordings

Keyboard events may only be captured as high-level interaction metadata, for example “Enter pressed” or “Escape pressed”, and must not contain typed characters.

## Console Logs

The extension shall capture console output generated while the extension is active on the page.

Captured console data shall include:

* Timestamp
* Log level
* Message text after sanitization
* Source, if available

The console log buffer shall be limited to the latest 100 entries.

Console logs shall be sanitized before being written to the JSON export.

## JavaScript Errors

The extension shall capture JavaScript runtime errors and unhandled promise rejections generated while the extension is active on the page.

Captured error data shall include:

* Timestamp
* Error message after sanitization
* Error type
* Stack trace, if available and sanitized
* Source file, line, and column, if available

The error buffer shall be limited to the latest 50 entries.

## Network Request Metadata

The extension shall capture network request metadata for requests made while the extension is active.

Captured network data shall include:

* Timestamp
* HTTP method
* Request URL after sanitization
* Request type, if available
* Response status code, if available
* Request duration, if available
* Error state, if applicable

The network buffer shall be limited to the latest 200 metadata entries.

The extension shall not store:

* Cookies
* Authorization headers
* API keys
* Access tokens
* Refresh tokens
* Session IDs
* Request bodies by default
* Response bodies by default
* Full request headers by default
* Full response headers by default

Query parameters shall either be removed completely or sanitized using an allowlist.

## Privacy and Data Protection

The generated JSON file must not contain personal data, credentials, secrets, tokens, or customer-specific confidential information.

Sensitive data protection shall use multiple layers:

1. Data minimization: only collect information required for debugging.
2. Allowlist-based collection: prefer explicitly allowed fields over broad data collection.
3. Field-level exclusion: never collect known sensitive fields.
4. Sanitization: remove or mask sensitive patterns before writing the JSON file.
5. Final validation: check the generated JSON before download.

Regex-based sanitization may be used as an additional protection mechanism but must not be the only protection mechanism.

The sanitizer shall remove or mask at least:

* Email addresses
* Phone numbers
* Access tokens
* Refresh tokens
* Bearer tokens
* API keys
* Session IDs
* Cookies
* Authorization headers
* Password-like fields
* Secret-like fields
* Personal identifiers in query parameters

## JSON Export

When the user clicks the bug report button, the extension shall generate a structured JSON file and trigger a local download.

The JSON file shall include:

* Schema version
* Page metadata
* Browser metadata
* Last captured user interactions
* Captured console logs
* Captured JavaScript errors
* Captured network request metadata
* Sanitization summary
* Known capture limitations

The JSON structure shall be stable and versioned to allow later automated processing.

## User Control

The export shall only be triggered by explicit user action.

Before the JSON file is downloaded, the extension should show a short summary of the information that will be included in the bug report.

The user shall be able to cancel the export.

The captured event history shall remain local to the browser and shall only be written to a downloadable JSON file after explicit user action.

## Performance Requirements

The extension must not noticeably slow down normal browser usage.

The extension shall avoid high-frequency event logging.

Scroll and resize events shall be throttled.

The extension shall not traverse or serialize the full DOM on every event.

The extension shall not store large objects, screenshots, videos, request bodies, or response bodies.

The initial implementation shall use in-memory storage per tab.

Persistent storage shall only be used if reload-resilient bug capture is required in a later version.

## Capture Limitations

The extension is only required to include data captured while it was active on the current page.

The extension is not required to reconstruct console logs, network requests, UI events, or errors that happened before the extension was initialized.

The extension is not required to capture data from browser-internal pages, restricted pages, or cross-origin iframes where browser extension access is limited.

## Acceptance Criteria

* A user can click the browser extension button and download a JSON bug report.
* The JSON contains the current URL, user agent, viewport size, screen resolution, scroll position, timestamp, and schema version.
* The extension keeps a local in-memory ring buffer of the last 50 relevant interactions or the last 5 minutes, whichever is smaller.
* The JSON contains the captured interaction history.
* The JSON contains captured console logs generated while the extension was active.
* The JSON contains captured JavaScript errors generated while the extension was active.
* The JSON contains captured network request metadata generated while the extension was active.
* The JSON does not contain cookies, authorization headers, access tokens, refresh tokens, API keys, passwords, session IDs, request bodies, or response bodies.
* Query parameters are either removed or sanitized.
* Form input values are not stored.
* Typed characters are not stored.
* Mouse movement and raw pointer movement are not stored.
* Scroll and resize events are throttled.
* The JSON file contains a sanitization summary.
* The JSON file contains known capture limitations.
* The export can be cancelled before download.
